      "reason": "官方文档指预测样本均值的常数模型，不能误写为目标为常数的情况。"
    },
    {
      "old": "**English reference answer（笔记自拟）**: The momentum plots show at most a weak positive pattern, and the simple and multiple regressions estimate imprecise slopes. The reported positive OOS $R^2$ belongs to the joint three-predictor model, so it cannot be attributed to momentum alone. Forecast accuracy also omits direction, trading costs, portfolio constraints, and risk. I would change the conclusion only if a prespecified momentum-only rule delivered stable positive OOS performance and useful net portfolio results on later untouched dates.",
      "new": "**English reference answer（笔记自拟）**:\n\nThe momentum plots show at most a weak positive pattern, and the simple and multiple regressions estimate imprecise slopes.\n\nThe reported positive OOS $R^2$ belongs to the joint three-predictor model, so it cannot be attributed to momentum alone.\n\nForecast accuracy also omits direction, trading costs, portfolio constraints, and risk.\n\nI would change the conclusion only if a prespecified momentum-only rule delivered stable positive OOS performance and useful net portfolio results on later untouched dates.\n",
